  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_039: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) achieves 0.725 acc / 0.685 F1. Prior evidence shows weighted fusion outperforms concat with pca_n2000+resnet50 (config_019: 0.639 vs config_018: 0.619), but this gap was only ~2% and in a lower-performance regime. Config_038 is a single-variable change (weighted→concat) from the best config, directly testing whether the weighted-fusion advantage persists when combined with transformer aggregation and the stronger ViT-L image encoder. If concat performs comparably, it confirms the design is robust and simplifies the search; if weighted is clearly superior, it validates the current best and narrows the design space. Under a limited budget, this targeted exploitation of the most promising region is more informative than exploring a new axis (e.g., scgpt, which config_051 showed to be poor) or a less-connected variant."
}

